Course.start({"num":16,"unit":3,"slug":"m16-ser-estar","minutes":45,"title":"Ser y estar","subtitle":"Choosing the right *to be*","lede":"Two verbs, one English meaning. *Ser* tells what something **is**; *estar* tells where it is and how it **is doing**. Choosing the right one can change what you mean.","recap":"You've learned both verbs: **ser** (*soy, eres, es, somos, sois, son*) in Module 8, and **estar** (*estoy, estás, está, estamos, estáis, están*) last time.","context":{"title":"Caminante, no hay camino","place":"Soria, Castilla y León","text":"In 1912 the poet **Antonio Machado** published *Campos de Castilla* (*Fields of Castile*), poems written while he taught French at a high school in the small city of Soria. In a new edition in **1917**, he added a set of very short poems. One of them became one of the most quoted lines in the Spanish language:\n\n{{Caminante, no hay camino, se hace camino al andar.}}\n\n*Traveler, there is no road; you make the road by walking.*\n\nMachado's idea fits this module. Some things describe who you **are**, like where you're from or what you're like: that's **ser**. Others describe where you **are** on the road right now, and how you feel along the way: that's **estar**. {{Soy estudiante. Estoy en el camino.}}"},"learn":[{"title":"Ser or estar? Two memory tricks","text":"**Ser** is for what something *is*: think **DOCTOR**. **Estar** is for where and how something is: think **PLACE**. (\"How you feel and where you are, that's when you use estar.\")","table":{"head":["SER · DOCTOR","ESTAR · PLACE"],"rows":[["**D**escription: {{Es alto.}}","**P**osition: {{Está sentado.}} (seated)"],["**O**ccupation: {{Soy estudiante.}}","**L**ocation: {{Estoy en Soria.}}"],["**C**haracteristic: {{Es simpática.}}","**A**ction in progress: {{Estoy estudiando.}} (Module 24)"],["**T**ime and date: {{Son las tres.}}","**C**ondition: {{La sopa está fría.}}"],["**O**rigin: {{Somos de Ohio.}}","**E**motion: {{Están contentos.}}"],["**R**elationship: {{Es mi tía.}}",""]]}},{"title":"Same adjective, different meaning","text":"Some adjectives mean something different with each verb. **Ser** describes what someone is like; **estar** describes how they are at the moment.","table":{"head":["with SER","with ESTAR"],"rows":[["{{Es aburrido.}} He's boring.","{{Está aburrido.}} He's bored."],["{{Es listo.}} He's clever.","{{Está listo.}} He's ready."],["{{Es malo.}} He's bad (a bad person).","{{Está malo.}} He's sick. (food: it tastes bad)"],["{{Es rico.}} He's rich.","{{Está rico.}} It's delicious."],["{{Es nervioso.}} He's a nervous person.","{{Está nervioso.}} He's nervous right now."]]}},{"title":"Events use ser","text":"Location usually takes **estar**, but an **event** (a party, a game, a concert, a class) uses **ser** to say where and when it *takes place*.","examples":[["Mi casa está en la calle Mayor.","My house is on Main Street. (location: estar)"],["La fiesta es en mi casa.","The party is at my house. (event: ser)"],["¿Dónde es el partido? Es en el estadio.","Where is the game? It's at the stadium."],["La mesa es de madera.","The table is (made of) wood. (material: ser)"]]}],"tasks":[{"id":"t1","type":"sort","title":"Ser or estar?","intro":"Which verb belongs in the blank?","cats":["ser","estar"],"pick":10,"items":[["Mi madre ___ doctora.",0,"Occupation: **ser**."],["Nosotros ___ en la biblioteca.",1,"Location: **estar**."],["Hoy ___ martes.",0,"Day and date: **ser**."],["Ellos ___ muy cansados.",1,"Condition: **estar**."],["Machado ___ de Sevilla.",0,"Origin: **ser**."],["La sopa ___ fría.",1,"Condition right now: **estar**."],["Ana ___ mi prima.",0,"Relationship: **ser**."],["Yo ___ contento hoy.",1,"Emotion: **estar**."],["La fiesta ___ en mi casa.",0,"An event: **ser**."],["Mi casa ___ cerca de la escuela.",1,"Location of a thing: **estar**."],["___ las dos de la tarde.",0,"Time: **ser**."],["Tú ___ muy alto.",0,"Description: **ser**."]],"hints":["DOCTOR → ser: Description, Occupation, Characteristic, Time, Origin, Relationship.","PLACE → estar: Position, Location, Action, Condition, Emotion.","Events (parties, games) use **ser** for where they happen."]},{"id":"t2","type":"select","title":"Choose the right form","intro":"Choose the correct form of *ser* or *estar*.","items":[{"s":"Yo {soy|estoy|es} de Pensilvania."},{"s":"Mis amigos {están|son|estamos} en el parque."},{"s":"¿Cómo {estás|eres|está} hoy?"},{"s":"Nosotros {somos|estamos|son} hermanos."},{"s":"La clase {es|está|son} a las nueve."},{"s":"El concierto {es|está|están} en el teatro."},{"s":"Uf, {estoy|soy|está} muy aburrido en esta clase.","en":"Ugh, I'm so bored in this class."},{"s":"Mi abuelo {es|está|eres} muy simpático."}],"hints":["*¿Cómo estás?* asks how you feel; *¿Cómo eres?* asks what you're like.","Events (*el concierto*) use **ser**."]},{"id":"t3","type":"cloze","title":"Complete the postcard","intro":"Write the correct form of *ser* or *estar*.","items":["¡Hola, Sara! Yo [estoy] en Soria con mi familia.","Soria [es] una ciudad pequeña y bonita.","Nuestro hotel [está] cerca del río.","Hoy [es] sábado y [son] las cinco.","Mis padres [están] muy contentos.","Mi hermano [está] cansado porque caminamos mucho.","La comida aquí [es|está] deliciosa.","¡Tú [eres] mi mejor amiga!"],"hints":["Where someone is → **estar**. What a place is like → **ser**.","*La comida es deliciosa* (in general) or *está deliciosa* (this meal): both are correct!"]},{"id":"t4","type":"match","title":"Same word, new meaning","intro":"Match each sentence (tap to hear it) with its meaning.","pairs":[["Es aburrido.","He's boring."],["Está aburrido.","He's bored."],["Es listo.","He's clever."],["Está listo.","He's ready."],["Es rico.","He's rich."],["La sopa está rica.","The soup is delicious."],["Es malo.","He's a bad person."],["Está malo.","He's sick."]],"hints":["**Ser** = what someone is like. **Estar** = how they are right now."]},{"id":"t5","type":"errors","title":"Fix the mistakes","intro":"Each sentence uses the wrong verb. Tap it, then write the right form.","items":[{"s":"Mi padre está profesor.","bad":"está","fix":"es","why":"Occupation: **ser**."},{"s":"Yo soy en la cafetería.","bad":"soy","fix":"estoy","why":"Location: **estar**."},{"s":"Ellas son muy cansadas hoy.","bad":"son","fix":"están","why":"A condition today: **estar**."},{"s":"La fiesta está en el gimnasio.","bad":"está","fix":"es","why":"An event: **ser**."},{"s":"Hoy está lunes.","bad":"está","fix":"es","why":"Days and dates: **ser**."}],"hints":["Ask: DOCTOR or PLACE?"]},{"id":"t6","type":"listen","title":"Why that verb?","intro":"Listen to each sentence. Why does it use *ser* or *estar*?","questions":[{"say":"Mi tía es enfermera en un hospital.","choices":[["occupation (ser)",true],["location (estar)",false],["emotion (estar)",false],["time (ser)",false]]},{"say":"Estamos en la playa.","choices":[["location (estar)",true],["origin (ser)",false],["description (ser)",false],["condition (estar)",false]]},{"say":"El concierto es en el estadio.","choices":[["an event (ser)",true],["location of a thing (estar)",false],["emotion (estar)",false],["origin (ser)",false]]},{"say":"¡Qué rica está la paella!","choices":[["how it tastes right now (estar)",true],["it's expensive (ser)",false],["where it is (estar)",false],["what it's made of (ser)",false]]}],"hints":["DOCTOR for *ser*, PLACE for *estar*, and events take *ser*."]},{"id":"s1","type":"speak","title":"Machado's line","intro":"Listen to the famous line, then record yourself saying it.","items":[{"s":"Caminante, no hay camino, se hace camino al andar."},{"s":"Soy de Scranton, pero ahora estoy en Madrid."}]}],"build":{"heading":"Una postal","prompt":"Write a postcard (**at least 6 sentences**) to a friend from a real or imagined trip. Say where you are, what the place is like, who you're with and how everyone feels. Use **ser** at least twice and **estar** at least twice.","model":"{{¡Hola, Marcos!}} {{Estoy en Sevilla con mi familia.}} {{Sevilla es una ciudad muy bonita y antigua.}} {{Nuestro hotel está cerca de la catedral.}} {{Hoy es domingo y hace mucho calor.}} {{Mis padres están contentos, pero mi hermana está cansada.}} {{¡La comida es deliciosa!}} {{Hasta pronto, Ana}}","placeholder":"¡Hola…! Estoy en…","reqs":[{"t":"At least 6 sentences","sentences":6},{"t":"**ser** at least twice","re":"\\b(soy|eres|es|somos|sois|son)\\b","min":2},{"t":"**estar** at least twice","re":"\\b(estoy|estás|está|estamos|estáis|están)\\b","min":2},{"t":"Where you are (*estoy en…*)","re":"\\b(estoy|estamos)\\s+en\\b"},{"t":"A feeling with estar","re":"\\b(estoy|estás|está|estamos|estáis|están)\\s+(muy\\s+|un\\s+poco\\s+)?(content|trist|cansad|enferm|nervios|aburrid|enojad|preocupad|ocupad|emocionad|tranquil|bien|mal)\\p{L}*"}]},"reflect":{"q":"Machado wrote that we make our road by walking. Think of one thing about who you **are** (*ser*) that you hope never changes, and one thing about where you **are** right now (*estar*) that you hope will change or grow this year.","placeholder":"Something about who I am… Something about where I am right now…"},"further":{"id":"x1","type":"translate","title":"Challenge: choose and translate","items":[{"en":"I'm ready.","es":["[yo] estoy {listo|lista}"]},{"en":"She's clever.","es":["[ella] es lista"]},{"en":"The game is at the school.","es":["el partido es en la escuela"]},{"en":"We're from Spain, but we're in Mexico.","es":["[nosotros] somos de españa pero estamos en méxico","[nosotras] somos de españa pero estamos en méxico"]}]},"culture":"**¿Sabías?** Machado's line became famous all over again in 1969, when the Catalan singer **Joan Manuel Serrat** put the poem to music in the song *Cantares*.","unitTitle":"Mi vida diaria: el presente","code":"NzE5MS1FVE5BTklNQUM=","prev":"m15-estar.html","next":"m17-ir.html"});
